ARM 1 — SPECIFICATION TRACE: where the number six is load-bearing
==============================================================================
  docs/SPEC.md:240  FR32 [v2]                     names SIX epochs by name + the 30-day crisis window and 5-15d lead
                                                  -> NORMATIVE SOURCE. Everything below derives from this line.
  docs/SPEC.md:102  O5 [v2]                       'Six epochs, corpus 2005-2026'
                                                  -> ties the event count to the CORPUS BOUND — the two are stated together
  docs/SPEC.md:243  FR35 [v2]                     Table A = 7 subsets x 2 modes on 4 Hawkes epochs; Table B = 3 x 2 on 2 pre-2015
                                                  -> the 4/2 split of the six; changes the CONFIG COUNT (14)
  docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:756 D5(a,b)                LOEO; Table A 4 folds, Table B 6 folds; tables not comparable
                                                  -> FOLD COUNTS are literally the event counts
  docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:645 R4                     'Six positive events, 14 configurations, one calibration step'
                                                  -> the risk register's justification for pre-registration existing at all
  seraph/shared_types/fusion.py:27 EpochId        Literal of exactly 6 string ids
                                                  -> TYPE-LEVEL CLOSED SET. A 7th epoch is a type error until edited; shared_types is approval-gated, so this is the hardest gate.
  seraph/validation/epochs.py:23 EPOCH_BREAKS     6 (date, provenance) pairs; HAWKES_COVERED 4 / PRE_HAWKES 2
                                                  -> the only place dates live; OQ13 + OQ3 both flagged OPEN here
  seraph/validation/preregistration.py:24 EPOCHS  6-tuple duplicated from epochs.py; folds=len(EPOCHS)
                                                  -> feeds configuration_list() -> content_hash() -> the PRE-REG HASH

  MECHANICAL CONSEQUENCE of changing the count, in dependency order:
   1. EpochId Literal (approval-gated shared_types) must gain members
   2. EPOCH_BREAKS gains (date, provenance) rows -> OQ13 must close
   3. preregistration.EPOCHS changes -> configuration_list() changes
      -> content_hash() changes -> EVERY existing EvaluationRow's
         preRegistrationHash stops matching -> by D5(d) every existing
         result becomes NON-REPORTABLE until re-run.
   4. D5(b) fold counts change (Table B 6 -> N; Table A only if the
      new epoch has Hawkes coverage, i.e. onset >= 2017-02-09)
   5. FR35's '7 subsets x 2' / '3 subsets x 2' are unaffected — the
      CONFIG count is independent of the EVENT count.

  So the '6' controls: fold counts (D5b), a closed type (EpochId),
  the pre-registration hash (D5d), and the Table A/B partition.
  It does NOT control the 14 configurations.

