  READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING THE ROWS ABOVE:
   * N here is the number of ONSETS, i.e. independent events. The
     positive-day count 15N is NOT the sample size — days inside one
     lead window are near-perfectly correlated (phi ~ 0.997).
   * Power rises with N only if the added onsets are independent. Two
     onsets 30 days apart add ~1 event's worth of information, not 2.
   * The AAFT null is used for the curve because the circular-shift
     null is miscalibrated on a near-unit-root series — that is the
     measured finding in docs/evidence/EARLY-WARNING-POWER.md, not an
     assumption made here.

